# Line endings.
#
# The repository is worked on from Windows, where git is configured to check
# files out with CRLF. A shell script that reaches a Linux container that way
# fails on its own first line: the kernel reads "/bin/sh\r" as the interpreter
# and cannot find it. The container entrypoint is the one file where that
# turns a deploy into a crash loop, so these are pinned to LF.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
